  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Employability and Entrepreneurial Capability of Higher Technical Education Graduates</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By nurturing individuals with advanced degrees in vocational and technical fields (Master of Technology) and offering industry-academia linked programs to strengthen their entrepreneurial and employment capabilities, we aim to contribute to Rwanda&apos;s development goal of creating 1.5 million quality jobs.Enhance the efficiency of program implementation by addressing the deficiencies of individual projects, strengthen the sustainability of individual project outcomes, and provide opportunities for the final beneficiaries (students) to develop professional competencies that align with the demands of the local labor market.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development and implementation of industry-academia collaborative Bachelor and pilot Master programs in IT, Production, and Electrical fields, establishment and operation of entrepreneurship, research incubation programs (including seed funding and consulting), enhancement of operational environments for Bachelor and Master and incubation programs (such as equipment support), strengthening of operational capabilities for Bachelor and Master and incubation programs (including stakeholder capacity building through local and invited training), and project management (including monitoring and evaluation).</narrative>
  </description>
